Z||000000||fiero56||10-01-2001||07:18 PM||||I first noticed the 2.8 in my '86SE making a slight rattle at 1800rpm under neutral throttle. Today I noticed it has progressed to 1500-2500(+???)rpm and occurs under most all throttle loads. About all it can be is a loose rod/main. Before anything gets irrepairable(out of round), I plan to hit it.<P>I've been planning to perform a mild rebuild of this engine, but not this soon. I've got a spare crank I will have cut. I will also get a set of main+rod bearings, hi-vol oil pump, timing chain, and related gaskets.<P>Anything I am forgetting? I am planning to accomplish this in a saturday afternoon(should be very possible). I had planned on honing the cylinder walls, new rings, and recon'd heads, but maybe later. Engine/clutch have 107K original miles, but clutch is still solid, and will become an auto in the coming months, so I don't plan to mess with the clutch set. Water-pump was replaced about 3 months ago.<BR>I've thought about rod bolts, but I don't plan to pull rods to have new bolts pressed in, hopefully the stockers will last, any thoughts on that?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||10-01-2001||07:52 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fiero56:<BR><B>I first noticed the 2.8 in my '86SE making a slight rattle at 1800rpm under neutral throttle. Today I noticed it has progressed to 1500-2500(+???)rpm and occurs under most all throttle loads. About all it can be is a loose rod/main. Before anything gets irrepairable(out of round), I plan to hit it.<P>I've been planning to perform a mild rebuild of this engine, but not this soon. I've got a spare crank I will have cut. I will also get a set of main+rod bearings, hi-vol oil pump, timing chain, and related gaskets.<P>Anything I am forgetting? I am planning to accomplish this in a saturday afternoon(should be very possible). I had planned on honing the cylinder walls, new rings, and recon'd heads, but maybe later. Engine/clutch have 107K original miles, but clutch is still solid, and will become an auto in the coming months, so I don't plan to mess with the clutch set. Water-pump was replaced about 3 months ago.<BR>I've thought about rod bolts, but I don't plan to pull rods to have new bolts pressed in, hopefully the stockers will last, any thoughts on that?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hate to say it, but if you are not going to do the full job, you may miss something and loose what you are investing...<BR>I had a strange rattle that I thought was a lifter...<BR>Turns out it was a piston skirt, and when it failed, it cracked the cylinder wall...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||10-01-2001||08:30 PM||||Hey! Don't scare me like that <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.<P>I'm hoping it is something simple like a bearing on the bottom end. Since the sound only occurs once the engine has thoroughly warmed up(10-15 minutes) I am assuming it is due to the oil being thinner. Piston skirts and such closer to the top end heat up much faster so I would think they would make noise soon after start-up. Just yesterday I saw pictures of what a broken ring did to a piston, now I have that image floating in the back of my head <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.||||reg||1
